WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.054
Wednesday Addams has gotten a makeover, and
some vocal fans aren't happy.

00:00:05.054 --> 00:00:09.719
In their opinion, her name should be changed
to Mary Sue Addams instead.

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:13.990
With her deadpan wit, gothic wardrobe, and
affection for all things macabre, Wednesday

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.940
Addams is an outcast icon.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.980
Popularized by Christina Ricci's portrayal
of the character in the Addams Family films

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.110
of the '90s, the teenage nightmare has recently
received a modern makeover.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:29.660
Now played by Jenna Ortega in Netflix's Wednesday,
the character sports a fresh new fringe hairstyle,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.840
as well as some new priorities compared to
her predecessors.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.899
When Wednesday opens, Wednesday has just been
expelled from Nancy Reagan High School for

00:00:36.899 --> 00:00:39.660
unleashing piranhas on the water polo team.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.510
As a result, she enrolls at a new school called
Nevermore Academy.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.050
While this Edgar Allan Poe-inspired school
for outcasts may seem more her speed, Wednesday

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.710
nevertheless insists on staying away from
the pack and only focusing on her writing,

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.890
cello playing, and solving a mystery that
plagues the academy grounds.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:00.180
However, while Wednesday's many talents may
make for entertaining television, what some

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.790
are characterizing as a lack of realism has
soured certain viewers on Wednesday's character

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.659
in the show's early episodes.

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:11.439
For a self-described loner, Wednesday Addams
seems to participate in plenty of extracurriculars

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:12.444
in Wednesday.

00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:17.270
Before entering the halls of Nevermore, Wednesday
is an accomplished cellist, author, and fencer.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.770
She then continues to prove her talents in
each of these activities as the series progresses.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.570
Certain viewers, however, have criticized
Wednesday's competency in her wide variety

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.500
of interests as presented at the show's outset,
describing her as an archetypical "Mary Sue."

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.250
In fiction, the "Mary Sue" archetype is a
main character who is incredibly well-liked

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:37.280
and competent — and without any noticeable
flaws.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.070
In a thread they started on the Netflix subreddit
about the first three episodes of Wednesday,

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:41.947
one user wrote:

00:01:48.588 --> 00:01:50.832
On the same thread, another redditor replied:

00:01:57.845 --> 00:02:01.190
Another reddit user wrote that the degree
to which they found Wednesday to be more of

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:05.670
a caricature than a three-dimensional character
made the show hard to watch for them.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.710
Additionally, people on Twitter have described
the character as a Mary Sue explicitly.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:13.420
That said, most of these impressions seem
to be based on the start of the series, and

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.989
have elicited plenty of pushback against this
idea that Wednesday fits the so-called Mary

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:19.050
Sue archetype.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:23.530
In response to criticism that Wednesday Addams
is a supposed Mary Sue at the start of Wednesday,

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.849
a number of users online have countered that
Wednesday becomes plenty three-dimensional

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:29.217
as the show continues.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.400
"Where are your whiskers?"

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:34.340
"Ask again and you'll be down to eight lives."

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.940
For example, in a Reddit thread that criticized
Wednesday based on the first three episodes

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.045
of the new Netflix show, one user countered,

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:49.360
Another user similarly argued that Wednesday's
independence ultimately proves to be a character

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.780
flaw down the line.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:55.099
On Twitter, people have also written that
Wednesday does not qualify as a Mary Sue.

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:59.030
As talented as Wednesday is, her character
still runs into conflict as Wednesday continues

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.129
past its opening few episodes.

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:04.930
Wednesday is constantly challenged, especially
when no one believes a fellow Nevermore Academy

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.950
student by the name of Rowan was murdered.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.090
Her biggest hurdle, meanwhile, is her struggle
with empathy.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.868
Wednesday's true failing, as it turns out,
is her inability to connect with those around her.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:17.970
How she progresses through this struggle ultimately
becomes one of the show's focal points.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.150
While initially the ultimate outsider, Wednesday
overcomes her internal struggle by accepting

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.410
people into her life by Season 1's end.

